import Mathlib

/-!
# A single frequency band for the mean square of moving character sums
The estimate holds for every dyadic upper endpoint and every character at a polylogarithmic
modulus, with the principal term subtracted. The rectangular window is the actual interval
exp(u) < n ≤ exp(u+δ). Fourier inversion with both boundaries, summation by parts,
and explicit high-frequency integration justify the two discarded ranges.
The middle integral is left visible in the statement.
    
The unconditional Siegel-Walfisz input below is adapted from goldbach-proofs PR 1667,
813ca8c4a3e6ab6ef53180fc5a2c56275a19db88, with the original OpenAI credits preserved.
Finite multiplicative-character Parseval is adapted from LogTruSoul, goldbach-proofs
PR 2829, cfde193e18afc4e0ffac53868d514142e908cd36, derived from PR 2486,
f3613cf846dfb3e7fe7d04fe6ce51c6ee25e7d4f, Apache-2.0.
-/

/-!
# Major-arc estimates for the prime logarithmic sum

The general finite estimates below are from DFQDZZ, goldbach-proofs PR #316,
revision e4ab24712555ae8c2c926adf19d368a9fb392c35 (Apache-2.0).

The analytic material in the namespaces OAI.LargePrimeGaps is selected and adapted
from OpenAI's openai/math, lean/OAI/NumberTheory/PrimeGaps, at revision
f5702854040e97fa7675c21ba37a9608f5f92dd3, licensed under Apache 2.0 (see LICENSE).
It is specialized to the declarations required for the small-modulus estimate and
ported from toolchain 4.34.1 to the version locked by this repository.
-/

